  "question": {
    "text": "A galvanometer having internal resistance $10 \\Omega$ requires 0.01 A for a full scale deflection. To convert this galvanometer to a voltmeter of full-scale deflection at $120 \\mathrm{V}$, we need to connect a resistance of",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KP9ti",
      "text": "$11990 \\Omega$ in series",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oF1XH",
      "text": "$11990 \\Omega$ in parallel",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GLsUM",
      "text": "$12010 \\Omega$ in series",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hqyos",
      "text": "$12010 \\Omega$ in parallel",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Resistance $R=\\frac{V}{i_{g}}-G=\\frac{120}{0.01}-10$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n&=12000-10 \\\\\r\nR=11990 \\Omega\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\nTo convert a galvanometer into a voltmeter, high resistance should connect in series.",
